      "input": "Thanks *he said to them, after which he decides to give them back the boots*\nYou'll need them more than me",
      "outcome": "success",
      "exception": null,
      "narration": "Nicco's words hang in the air between them, perhaps slightly odd given that the boots remain on Mira's person and no exchange has occurred. She glances down at her own feet, then back at him with a restrained, skeptical expression, smelling a pinch of dried something from one pocket before she speaks.\n\n\"You're giving me something I already have?\" she says, voice matter-of-fact rather than accusing. \"Or you've mistaken who carried what.\" She does not step back or forward, merely waits, copper-brown hair catching the daylight of the square, her posture that of someone accustomed to odd encounters near The Coined Lie and unhurried in sorting them out.",
